{"page":"CNP","gene":"CNP","accession":"P09543","protein":"Myelin protein CNP","length":421,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"P09543-1","name":"CNP2","synonyms":["DNAII"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Mitochondrial and more broadly expressed isoform that can catalyze the hydrolysis of the 3'-phosphodiester bond of 2',3'-cyclic nucleotides to produce 2'-nucleotides. However, the physiological relevance of this activity is unclear (By similarity). In myelinating oligodendrocytes, may protect axons from injury by hydrolyzing 2',3'-cyclic nucleotides, thereby reducing levels of 2',3'-cAMP, a mitochondrial toxin that promotes mitochondrial permeability transition pore opening, and generating adenosine, a neuroprotectant (PubMed:38117830)"},{"topic":"Function","text":"(Microbial infection) SARS-CoV-2 induces the mitochondrial release of reactive oxygen species (ROS) into the cytoplasm which benefits its replication. Because it regulates the mitochondrial permeability transition pore (mPTP) and the associated release of ROS, CNP antagonizes SARS-CoV-2 replication"},{"topic":"Caution","text":"Isoform-specific mitochondrial localization, as well as the function of the mitochondrial transit peptide demonstrated for the rat protein, are not confirmed with the human protein"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000393892.8"],"refseq":["NM_033133.5"],"refseqProteins":["NP_149124.3"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-P09543-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P09543-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":87.3,"plddt":[[0,24],[50,4],[70,3],[90,59],[70,5],[90,44],[70,1],[90,41],[70,4],[90,35],[70,9],[50,3],[70,4],[90,9],[70,3],[90,63],[70,11],[90,15],[70,1],[90,16],[70,7],[90,15],[70,1],[90,21],[70,2],[50,2],[0,19]]}},"features":[{"type":"Transit peptide","start":1,"end":20,"description":"Mitochondrion"},{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":20,"description":"(Microbial infection) N20aa; prevents the interaction with HI